    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0863" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/2157: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-04T01:00:00+03:00">May 4, 1939—1
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—7 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Foreign Office communiqué issued shortly after midnight states that
                        Litvinov has been relieved at his own
                    request of his duties as <pb facs="0864" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/> Commissar for
                    Foreign Affairs, and that his place will be taken by Molotov who will continue as Chairman of the Soviet of People’s
                    Commissars.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
